0071:     Move each source pixel toward the separator when it matches its aligned reference pixel, otherwise to the far edge.
0072: 
0073:     Input structure:
0074:     - A single full separator line is part of a rectangular frame; the frame's
0075:       extra cells mark the reference side.
0076:     - On the reference side, one row or column of colored pixels is aligned
0077:       with one row or column of source pixels on the opposite side.
0078:     - Each side has its own dominant background color.
0079: 
0080:     Rule:
0081:     - Compare each source pixel with the reference pixel on the same row or column.
0082:     - If their colors match, place the source pixel in the cell adjacent to the
0083:       separator on the source side.
0084:     - If their colors differ, place the source pixel on the far outer edge along
0085:       the same row or column.
0086:     - Erase the original source pixels to the source-side background; keep the
0087:       frame and reference pixels unchanged.
